# Manager - Strategic Research Group

London, United Kingdom

Apply

Job ID
:   11173BR

Location
:   London, United Kingdom

Job Family
:   Business teams

Practice Area
:   Know-how, library and training

Job Type
:   Permanent

Working Arrangement
:   Hybrid

## Job description

We have an exciting opportunity for a **Manager - Strategic Research Group** to join our **Research and Library team**, based in A&O Shearman's London office.   

**Research and Library team - London**   

Global Research and Library proactively serves internal and external clients with trusted, actionable and technology-enabled intelligence and resources across nearly 50 offices. The department provides four key services:

1. Library (global service): firm wide support in procurement and management of information resources.
2. Research (global service): transactional day-to-day research support and a bespoke strategic research service.
3. Global community liaison: guidance and support to local research and library teams through the development and management of global systems; provision of advice, expertise and coordination of projects.
4. Client services: contribution to client-facing products and the development of A&O Shearman Research and Library branded products.


**What you will do**   

The Strategic Research Group provides in-depth, bespoke analysis and research support to client teams and business development. They work across the global firm, supporting both management initiatives that drive new business opportunities for the firm and client teams as needed. SRG are embedded into the business and build close relationships with partners, sector and practice leads and BD teams; understanding the needs of BD and client teams and providing analysis that drives new business opportunities, shape strategic initiatives and support directly on live matters.  

The Strategic Research Manager will seek to proactively engage with key stakeholders and establish close relationships. The post holder is tasked with understanding stakeholder needs and developing creative analysis to meet these. The Strategic Research Manager will proactively identify opportunities; liaise with fee earners and the Business Development community; offer their expertise and input in respect of the best use of our information assets; and determine the most relevant approach to support the firm’s analysis requirements.  

The Strategic Research Manager uses a variety of resources to provide considered, comprehensive research outputs that support the firm. This involves interpreting data, analyzing trends and writing reports as required.  
In detail the role involves:

* Producing detailed, insightful research and analysis that brings deep, timely insights to inform our internal clients and external clients of the firm;
* Building on the team’s existing relationships, as well as actively seeking to develop new relationships, with fee earners, senior BD and other key stakeholders across the firm;
* Taking responsibility as the expert for one or more sectors, as well as being a product expert, both in terms of different practices that the firm serves and key databases;
* Interviewing requesters to understand and scope their needs and requirements, proactively making suggestions as to how research requests and projects can be enhanced;
* Responsible for managing large research and analysis projects, from scoping to resourcing and delivery of the final output;
* Producing detailed reports that provide in-depth analysis of clients/sectors, highlighting business opportunities; potential impact on the firm and for clients;
* Inputting into external content and thought leadership for the firm. Developing ideas for topics that will impact clients; developing bespoke analysis to support hypothesis; writing content alongside Global Content Team.
* Selecting the appropriate resources – and on occasion identifying new resources – to address the needs of the business. This involves checking resources for accuracy, consistency and timeliness;
* Deliver inductions to senior lateral hires and newly promoted partners, to ensure that they understand the value of the function
* Collaborating with colleagues across the network on the development of research and analysis approaches, methodologies and final output;
* Contributing to the training of colleagues and act as a mentor, as and when required.

The post holder will both manage and contribute to a range of projects. Examples include:

* Identifying opportunities to use information assets to develop new SRG Research branded reports, as the business requires;
* Providing recommendations on research and analysis approach, the merits of different data sets in support of firm initiatives and projects;
* Building stakeholder engagement, designing products and testing them with users;
* Identifying key data providers and then working with colleagues to determine if the firm should invest in them;
* Assessing the cost (both monetary and in terms of staff time) of products and making recommendations on their implementation.


**What you will have** 

* Relevant professional experience as a research analyst or data analyst
* Direct management experience in an analysis and research setting;
* Excellent all-round analysis and research skills, covering business, sector and financial research;
* Ability to manage expectations and negotiate deadlines, along with strong organizational skills;
* Strong writing skills, including the ability to abstract and summarize complex arguments and draw conclusions that align to the firm’s interests and/or help to identify opportunities;
* Numerical fluency and the ability to present data in an effective way, either through graphics or text;
* Ability to build and develop relationships at all levels of the organization, including senior executive level, and have credibility as an expert;
* Strong technical skills in key financial products, particularly Capital IQ, Pitchbook, FactSet and LSEG;
* Experience of creating reports using the functionality of Word and PowerPoint, and competency in the use of Excel; Power BI experience a plus;
* A strategic and commercial mindset, with the ability to think about the bigger picture in respect of how research can play a part in supporting the success of the organization;
* Proactive approach with the ability to work on own initiative and manage own workload;
* Takes a collaborate approach on larger projects, engaging colleagues with the objective of delivering the best outcome for our internal clients.
* The Strategic Research Manager must be a credible, capable professional who is able to build and maintain productive relationships with senior lawyers, senior BD people, key stakeholders and peers across the business;
* Be confident in promoting Strategic Research Group Services to the firm, globally, and seek opportunities to do this; be comfortable presenting to senior executives in the business and at clients;
* Experience of, and an interest in, delivering research and analysis that offers real insight;
* The ability to interpret and then articulate key trends from raw data, e.g. deal data, and present it to our internal audience in an engaging, decision-ready format;
* Able to source and then evaluate third-party output in order to determine opportunities that match the firm’s interests, and proactively surface them to key stakeholders and explain why they are relevant;
* An interest in proactively taking ideas to our internal stakeholders and working with them to enhance our offering;
* Trusted to work on matters relating to the firm’s strategy and deliver research output to senior members of the firm (and ultimately seek to be retained by these people going forward);
* Financial modelling experience is desirable
* Strong sector and investment banking product knowledge, drawing on this knowledge to produce insightful output that can support the strategy of our practice groups and the firm.



---

*Should you require additional support at any stage of the recruitment process due to a disability or a health condition, please do not hesitate to contact a member of our recruitment team who will work with you to provide any adjustments as required.*  

*We are an equal opportunities recruiter and do not discriminate on the basis of race, colour, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, or any other protected characteristic.*



*We recognise that our people are our most valuable asset, which is reflected in the wide range of benefits that are available to our employees. Some of these benefits include: our occupational pension scheme, group income protection cover, private medical insurance, mental health resources and free apps, health and wellbeing services encompassing an onsite gym, wellbeing centre and GP service, emergency back-up care support, parental and special leave, holiday entitlement increasing with length of service, holiday trading, season ticket loans and online discounts and lifestyle management services.*



**Our approach to hybrid working seeks to combine and maximise the benefits of effective remote working with the benefits of being in the office. Our current hybrid working arrangements require office based working for a minimum of 60% of your time (**i.e.* *three days per week for a full time role) in accordance with our hybrid working policy.**



***NO AGENCIES PLEASE** - A&O Shearman does not accept unsolicited CVs. For further information, please see our UK Recruitment Agency Policy and our commitment to direct sourcing here.*

# Project Manager - Solar (Development)

Statkraft

In-person · London, England, GB

about 2 hours ago

#### Job Description

* Be responsible for developing ~ 1- 2 projects.
* Project management of our UK solar pipeline at all stages of project development from site identification through to pre-construction activity,
* Responsibility for management of project budgets and schedules from early-stage development to point of construction.
* Managing external service providers including Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA) and planning consultants, land agents, legal advisors and technical experts;
* Responsible for obtaining pre commencement planning condition discharge and further investigations as required;
* Responsible for obtaining any post consent planning variations;
* Identification of new solar projects, contributing to the development pipeline;
* Helping manage and coordinate our prospecting efforts for new sites
* Engage and negotiate agreements with landowners and representatives;
* Regular reporting on project progress, providing insightful risk and opportunity analysis to management;
* Stakeholder management (internal and external) and community engagement;
* Preparing and coordinating internal decision gate documentation.
* Engagement with the team and developing an understanding of the market.
* Engage with legal, land, compliance, health and safety, commercial, grid connection and engineering colleagues to integrate these specialisms in your projects;
* Coordinating with financial and technical colleagues to determine optimal strategy for the project with consideration of project risks;
* Support development and implementation of solar, energy storage and hydrogen projects as appropriate to the location;
* Analysing the market for solar energy and contributing to the strategy of the UK Solar Development Team

#### 

Statkraft is a leading company in hydropower internationally and Europe’s largest generator of renewable energy. The Group produces hydropower, wind power, solar power, gas-fired power and supplies district heating. Statkraft is a global company in energy market operations. Statkraft has over 5,300 employees in 21 countries. ...

# Solicitor - Associate - Commercial and Public Procurement

DAC Beachcroft is seeking an ambitious and commercial solicitor to join our highly successful Commercial & Procurement team. The team specialises in advising on procurement and contract law for complex, high value public sector projects across various sectors including health, education, transport, roads, nuclear and more.

## Key Responsibilities

The successful candidate will advise on a wide range of commercial and contractual matters including:

* Drafting, negotiating and advising on complex commercial contracts for public and private sector clients;
* Advising on outsourcing, managed services, technology, facilities management and strategic service delivery arrangements;
* Supporting public sector clients on major transformation, infrastructure and regeneration projects;
* Advising on PFI, PPP and other long-term partnering arrangements throughout their lifecycle, including contract management, contract variations, operational issues and expiry planning;
* Supporting clients in relation to PFI handback and operational contract matters;
* Advising on procurement strategy, procurement processes and procurement law compliance
* Providing practical, risk-based and commercially focused advice to clients;
* Building and maintaining strong client relationships;
* Supporting business development, thought leadership, training and client events.

## Skills, Knowledge and Expertise

We're looking for a qualified Solicitor with experience gained in a recognised commercial, projects, public sector or infrastructure practice. The following provides examples of desirable experience or interests;

* Drafting, negotiating and advising on commercial contracts;
* Experience of, or a genuine interest in developing expertise in public sector contracting;
* An ability to provide pragmatic, strategic advice on commercial arrangements, balancing legal risk with operational and service delivery objectives;
* An interest in working on multidisciplinary commercial projects and collaborating with specialists across a range of legal disciplines;
* Knowledge of UK public procurement law and procurement processes, or a  desire to develop specialist expertise in this area;
* A practical and commercial approach to problem solving;
* Good relationship management and communication skills;
* A good academic background and an appetite to take on responsibility and develop their practice.

## Why Join Us?

You will join one of the UK's leading public sector commercial and procurement practices, working alongside market-leading lawyers on matters that shape the delivery of public services and infrastructure across the country.  We are a friendly, informal team that respects work life balance but without compromising on quality for our clients.   

 The team is appointed to both the central government and wider public sector GCA Framework providing a broad range of work Across healthcare, government, transport, energy, technology, education, water, regeneration and wider public sector markets. We are involved in many of the most significant procurement, outsourcing and infrastructure projects currently being undertaken in the UK.   

 You will benefit from:

* Exposure to high-profile and complex work from day one;
* Direct client contact and responsibility appropriate to your experience;
* Structured development and mentoring from leading practitioners;
* Opportunities to develop specialist expertise in procurement, infrastructure and public sector contracting;
* A genuinely collaborative national team environment;
* Flexible and hybrid working arrangements;
* Competitive salary and comprehensive benefits package.

## About DAC Beachcroft

We are a leading international legal business with over 3,000 colleagues and a diverse range of capabilities. We are market leaders in insurance, health and real estate but with a full-service offering, including growing Financial Services and Tech capabilities. We represent a wide range of clients – from household names to government departments and NHS bodies. We act for nearly all of the top-20 UK and global insurers, we're market leaders in the provision of strategic, commercial and regulatory advice to providers and commissioners in the health sector, and in real estate we advise all of the UK’s top-five housebuilders.

We are a fast-growing international business with offices around the globe.  In addition to our 11 UK offices, we also have offices in Bogota, Buenos Aires, Dublin, Lima, Los Angeles, Hong Kong, Madrid, Mexico City, Milan, New York, Paris, Rome, Santiago de Chile, and Singapore plus a representative office in Miami and broad network of affiliations across the globe.

At DAC Beachcroft we are committed to and recognise the importance of equity, diversity and inclusion across the board, including and beyond the protected characteristics. We take decisions based solely on merit. We value, welcome and seek out people with different backgrounds and life experiences, perspectives, beliefs, ways of thinking and identities.

We are happy to talk flexible working with our Flex Forward scheme. We would encourage you to talk to us about our approach to flexible working during the hiring process if you would like to explore this further.   

**Note for Recruitment Agencies**  
DAC Beachcroft manages all vacancies via our in-house recruitment teams, prioritising direct sourcing and referrals. When external support is required, roles are released to selected agencies on our Preferred Supplier List (PSL).

Speculative CVs sent to any DAC Beachcroft employee without prior instruction from our recruitment teams (LLP and CSG) will not be accepted, and no fees will be payable.

For PSL queries, please contact: recruitment@dacbeachcroft.com or csgrecruitment@dacbeachcroft.com

